:: Underground Colosseum Landry Reaction
<<endevent>><<pass 5>>
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "pub">><<effects>><<npc Landry>><<person1>><<speechresolve>>
Landry finishes counting the money in the till before looking at you. "Still fighting, then."
<br><br>
<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
	<<case "meek">>"I need the money," you say, keeping your hands below the table.
	<<case "shy">>"I... still need the money," you say.
	<<case "polite">>"I know you warned me about the place, but I still need the money," you say.
	<<case "confident">>"I'm <<colosseumRankName>>-rank now. I'm doing fine," you say.
	<<case "bratty">>You pull out the chair opposite <<him>> and sit down. "You knew I wasn't going to stop."
	<<case "docile">>"I know you wanted me to stop," you say. "I still need the money."
	<<case "cruel">>"They keep paying me, so I keep fighting," you say.
	<<default>>"I'm <<colosseumRankName>>-rank now," you say.
<</switch>>
<br><br>
<<if $xchange.colosseum.injuryDays gt 0>>
	"I can see that the fights are getting worse." Landry looks at the bruises and cuts on your face.
<</if>>
"I hoped you'd lose interest before you got this far," <<he>> says.
<br><br>
<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
	<<case "meek">>"Do you know who runs the Colosseum?" you ask.
	<<case "shy">>"Do you know who runs it?" you ask quietly.
	<<case "polite">>"Can I ask who actually runs the Colosseum?" you ask.
	<<case "confident">>"You know more about the place than I do. Who runs it?" you ask.
	<<case "bratty">>"So who runs it?" you ask. "You must know something."
	<<case "docile">>"If you can tell me, who runs the Colosseum?" you ask.
	<<case "cruel">>"Who runs it? Give me a name," you say.
	<<default>>"Who actually runs the Colosseum?" you ask.
<</switch>>
<br><br>
Landry shakes <<his>> head. "I only knew how to get through the door. I gave you the passphrase, and that was everything I had. If someone claims they know more, find out what they want from you before you trust them."
<<set $xchange.colosseum.contacts to $xchange.colosseum.contacts | 1>><<colosseumHeat 2>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Pub]]>><<set $phase to 1>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Underground Colosseum Briar Reaction
<<endevent>><<pass 5>>
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "brothel">><<effects>><<npc Briar>><<person1>><<speechresolve>>
You tell Briar what rank you have reached. <<He>> picks up a notebook from beside the sofa and checks a page before answering.
"The higher your rank gets, the more people will pay to book you for a private match."
<br><br>
<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
	<<case "meek">>"Is that something I should worry about?" you ask.
	<<case "shy">>"Is that... bad?" you ask.
	<<case "polite">>"Should I be worried about that?" you ask.
	<<case "confident">>"You already have a reason for asking. What is it?" you ask.
	<<case "bratty">>"Are you planning to book me yourself, or sell the information to someone else?" you ask.
	<<case "docile">>"Do you need me to do something?" you ask.
	<<case "cruel">>"What are you planning to do with that information?" you ask.
	<<default>>"What are you checking?" you ask.
<</switch>>
<br><br>
Briar answers by asking how much the house charges for a private match. You tell <<him>>, and <<he>> writes it down.
<br><br>
Then <<he>> asks whether spectators in the private gallery can request a fighter by name, how early they need to book, and whether the fighter is paid by the desk or by the spectator.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Underground Colosseum Briar Reaction 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Underground Colosseum Briar Reaction 2
<<effects>><<speechresolve>>
<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
	<<case "meek">>"Why do you need all of this?" you ask.
	<<case "shy">>"Can I ask why you need all of this?" you ask.
	<<case "polite">>"I've answered your questions. I'd still like to know why you're asking," you say.
	<<case "confident">>"You've got enough answers from me. Now tell me why you need them," you say.
	<<case "bratty">>"I'm answering your questions. You can answer one of mine," you say. "Why do you need this?"
	<<case "docile">>"Do you need anything else from me?" you ask.
	<<case "cruel">>"Enough questions. Why do you need this?" you say.
	<<default>>"Why do you need this information?" you ask.
<</switch>>
<br><br>
Briar does not answer. <<He>> checks one last note, then closes the notebook.
<br><br>
<<if $xchange.colosseum.briarWatch and !$xchange.colosseum.briarReported and $xchange.colosseum.rank gte 4>>
	Briar keeps one finger between the pages. "You've been there long enough to recognise people from here."
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Give <<him>> the names|Briar Colosseum Names]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Say you haven't seen anyone|Briar Colosseum Silence]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<He>> puts the notebook beside the sofa. "Keep listening. If the private-match price changes, tell me."
	<<set $xchange.colosseum.contacts to $xchange.colosseum.contacts | 2>><<colosseumHeat 2>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Briar's Office]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<</if>>
<br>

:: Briar Colosseum Names
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "brothel">><<effects>><<pass 1>>
You give Briar the names of three workers you recognised at the Colosseum. <<He>> writes each one down, then underlines the second name twice.
"That one told me they were visiting their mother," <<he>> says. "Their mother died before they started working here."
<br><br>
Briar takes <span class="gold"><<printmoney 80000>></span> from the desk drawer and counts it into your hand.
<br><br>
"They're not in trouble for fighting," <<he>> says. "The problem is that they're working for another business in secret.
If they get hurt, disappear, or end up owing that place money, I may only find out after they've stopped coming to work."
<br><br>
<<He>> closes your fingers around the money. "I'll speak to them myself. If you recognise anyone else from here, bring me the name."
<<npcincr Briar love 1>><<glove>>
<<set $xchange.colosseum.briarReported to 1>><<set $xchange.colosseum.contacts to $xchange.colosseum.contacts | 2>>
<<money 80000 "colosseum">><<colosseumHeat 4 "Briar knows which of <<his>> staff are fighting, and why the house likes hiring them.">>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Briar's Office]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Briar Colosseum Silence
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "brothel">><<effects>><<pass 1>><<speechresolve>>
<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
	<<case "meek">>"I haven't seen anyone from here," you say.
	<<case "shy">>"I haven't recognised anyone," you say quietly.
	<<case "polite">>"I haven't recognised any of your workers there," you say.
	<<case "confident">>"If I had recognised someone, I'd tell you. I haven't," you say.
	<<case "bratty">>"I haven't seen anyone. That's the answer," you say.
	<<case "docile">>"No. I haven't seen anyone from here," you say.
	<<case "cruel">>"I haven't seen anyone. Stop asking," you say.
	<<default>>"I haven't seen anyone from the brothel," you say.
<</switch>>
<br><br>
Briar watches you for a few seconds, then opens the notebook and writes one short line. You cannot see what it says, and <<he>> does not ask again.
"Alright..." Briar sighs as <<he>> closes the notebook. "Keep listening anyway."
<<set $xchange.colosseum.briarReported to 2>><<set $xchange.colosseum.contacts to $xchange.colosseum.contacts | 2>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Briar's Office]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Underground Colosseum Bailey Reaction
<<endevent>><<pass 5>>
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "home">><<effects>><<npc Bailey>><<person1>><<speechresolve>>
<<set _titleMoment to $xchange.colosseum.rank gte 5 and $fame.scrap gte 800 and !$xchange.colosseum.baileyTitleUsed>>
Bailey holds out <<his>> hand before you finish saying the word Colosseum. "How much did they pay you?"
<br><br>
You tell <<him>> what the last fight paid. Bailey opens the rent ledger, writes the amount beside your name, and underlines it even though you have not given <<him>> any money.
<br><br>
<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
	<<case "meek">>"I haven't given it to you yet," you say.
	<<case "shy">>"Um... I haven't actually given you that money," you say.
	<<case "polite">>"You might want to wait until I've actually paid you before writing that down," you say.
	<<case "confident">>"You're counting it a little early," you say. "I still have it."
	<<case "bratty">>"You've already written down money you don't have," you say. "That's optimistic, even for you."
	<<case "docile">>"I'll pay what I owe," you say. "I just haven't given it to you yet."
	<<case "cruel">>"Don't count my money before I give it to you," you say.
	<<default>>"That money isn't yours yet," you say.
<</switch>>
<br><br>
"It will be." Bailey caps the pen.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Underground Colosseum Bailey Reaction 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Underground Colosseum Bailey Reaction 2
<<effects>>
<<set _titleMoment to $xchange.colosseum.rank gte 5 and $fame.scrap gte 800 and !$xchange.colosseum.baileyTitleUsed>>
<<if _titleMoment>>
	<<set $xchange.colosseum.baileyTitleUsed to 1>><<npcincr Bailey dom -1>>
	Bailey pauses before opening the ledger again.
	"Someone came to asking whether <span class="pink"><<colosseumName>></span> lived here. They had bet money on you and wanted to know whether you were eating properly."
	<br><br>
	Bailey writes another line beside your name.
	<br><br>
	"I told them you pay your rent on time. That's all a stranger needs to know about you." <<He>> points the pen at you. "Do not give anyone from that place this address."
<<else>>
	"You'll owe it, and I'd rather write it down once." <<He>> points the capped pen towards the door. "Shut that behind you."
<</if>>
<<set $xchange.colosseum.contacts to $xchange.colosseum.contacts | 4>><<colosseumHeat 2>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Bailey's Office]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Industrial Colosseum Recognition
<<set $daily.colosseumIndustrialRecognition to 1>>
<<set _fixCall to $xchange.colosseum.callbacks.fix and Time.days gte $xchange.colosseum.callbacks.fix>>
<<set _debtCall to $xchange.colosseum.debt gte 150000 and !$daily.colosseumDebtStreet>>
<<colosseumHuntLevel>>
<<if _fixCall>><<colosseumFixer>><<else>><<generate1>><<person1>><</if>>
<<if _fixCall>>
	<!-- One-shot: clear the callback here or it re-arms on every visit forever. -->
	<<set $xchange.colosseum.callbacks.fix to 0>>
	The <<person>> who paid you to deliberately lose a match is waiting where the alley narrows. This time <<he>> is wearing plain clothes and has brought another person with <<him>>.
	<br><br>
	"I told you I'd find out where you live," <<he>> says. "I did. I'm warning you here instead of going there. That's the last warning you get."
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Offer to pay <<him>> back|Colosseum Debt Pay]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Fight <<him>>|Colosseum Outside Challenge]]>><<violence 1>><<neutral 1>><<maninit>><</link>>
<<elseif _debtCall>>
	<<set $daily.colosseumDebtStreet to 1>>
	<<if $xchange.colosseum.debt gte 300000>><<colosseumHuntRaise 1 7>><</if>>
	A <<person>> steps out of a doorway and blocks the alley ahead of you. Another person stops behind you, leaving you between them.
	<br><br>
	"<span class="red"><<printmoney $xchange.colosseum.debt>></span>. That's your name in the book," the first one says. "You thought the debt stopped at the fucking door? Pay up."
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Offer to pay now|Colosseum Debt Pay]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Fight them|Colosseum Outside Challenge]]>><<violence 1>><<neutral 1>><<maninit>><</link>>
<<elseif _colosseumHunt gte 1 and random(1, 100) lte (20 + _colosseumHunt * 15)>>
	<<colosseumHuntNpc>>
	A <<person>> is waiting where the alley narrows. When <<he>> sees you, <<he>> steps across the path.
	<br><br>
	<<if _colosseumHunt gte 3>>
		"You're the fighter who opened the rooms and let people out through the delivery door," <<he>> says.
	<<else>>
		"Your name's on the list," <<he>> says. "The house sent me to collect."
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Colosseum Hunt Start]]>><<set $xchange.colosseum.huntReturn to "Industrial Alleyways">><</link>>
<<elseif $fame.scrap gte 400 and $xchange.colosseum.rank gte 4>>
	Three people are drinking beside the wall at the end of the alley. One of them recognises you and calls out your arena name.
	<br><br>
	<<He>> puts the bottle down and walks towards you. "C'mon, show us how well you fight without a referee."
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Show them|Colosseum Outside Challenge]]>><<violence 1>><<neutral 1>><<maninit>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Keep walking|Colosseum Outside Walk Away]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	A <<person>> loading crates onto a trolley stops working when you pass. <<He>> watches you until you reach the corner.
	<br><br>
	When you look back, <<he>> is pointing you out to someone standing in the loading-bay doorway.
	<<colosseumHeat 1>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Industrial Alleyways]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><<endevent>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Colosseum Betray Ambush
<<set $outside to 1>><<set $location to "alley">>
<<unset $xchange.colosseum.betrayAmbush>>
<<colosseumFixer>>
<<controlloss>><<violence 1>><<neutral 1>><<molested>>
<<strangeman2init>><<set $enemyanger += 120>>
<<effects>><<pass 1>>
<<set $xchange.colosseum.ambushReturn to "Industrial Alleyways">>
You have only walked a few steps from the Colosseum door when someone steps out from behind the skip.
<br><br>
It is the <<person>> who paid you to lose. You kept <<his>> money but won the fight anyway. <<He>> has been waiting for you outside.
"There are no Colosseum guards out here to stop me."<<stress 6>><<ggstress>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Underground Colosseum Ambush]]>><</link>>

:: Colosseum Debt Pay
<<effects>><<person1>><<pass 3>>
<<set _repayment to Math.min($money, $xchange.colosseum.debt)>>
<<if _repayment gt 0>>
	You count <span class="gold"><<printmoney _repayment>></span> into <<his>> hand. <<He>> counts it again before putting it away.
	<<money `-_repayment` "colosseumDebt">><<colosseumDebt `-_repayment`>>
	<br><br>
<</if>>
<<if $xchange.colosseum.debt is 0>>
	<<He>> strikes through the balance beside your name. "Paid. Keep the receipt. Some bastard tries to collect twice, you show them that."
	<<if $xchange.colosseum.ending is "disrupted">>
		<br><br>
		"That clears the money. Opening those rooms is another matter. Don't expect the house to call off its people."
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	<<if _repayment is 0>>You open your empty wallet. <<He>> knocks it aside.<br><br><</if>>
	<<set $xchange.colosseum.debtDeferred to 1>>
	"Still <span class="gold"><<printmoney $xchange.colosseum.debt>></span>. Bring it to the fighters' desk. Until then, your winnings come to us first. All of them, until the book's clear."
	<<stress 7>><<ggstress>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if $location is "colosseum">>
	<<link [[Return to the desk|Underground Colosseum Pit]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<link [[Leave|Industrial Alleyways]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><<endevent>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Colosseum Outside Walk Away
<<set $outside to 1>><<set $location to "alley">><<effects>><<person1>><<pass 3>>
You ignore them and keep walking. After a few steps, <<he>> starts shouting after you. The other two quickly join in.
<br><br>
<<switch random(1, 2)>>
	<<case 1>>
		"Look at it run away." <<He>> repeats your arena name in a mocking voice. "That's the fighter everyone keeps betting on?!"
	<<case 2>>
		"Come back and bend over for us instead." One of them puts their bottle down on the wall. "We've heard you'll do it for everyone else!"
<</switch>>
<br><br>
They keep shouting as you walk down the alley. By the time you reach the loading bay, they are loud enough that two workers stop what they are doing and look over at you.
<br><br>
<<if $exposed gte 1>>
	They also mock what you are wearing, calling out comments about your exposed body as you leave.<<fameexhibitionism 4 "none" true>>
<</if>>
<<colosseumBackDown 50>><<stress 8>><<ggstress>><<trauma 4>><<gtrauma>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Leave|Industrial Alleyways]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Colosseum Nurse Visit
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "school">><<schooleffects>><<effects>>
<<set $daily.colosseumNurse to 1>>
<<if $per_npc.school_nurse>><<loadNPC 0 school_nurse>><<else>><<generate1>><<saveNPC 0 school_nurse>><</if>><<person1>>
The nurse waits until you sit down, then checks the bruises along your arms and turns your face towards the lamp to see the cuts more clearly.
<br><br>
<<if $xchange.colosseum.injury gte 3>>
	"Tell me where it hurts." When you lift your arm, the movement makes you wince. <<He>> puts the pen down and draws the curtain around the bed. "Slowly. There's no hurry."
<<else>>
	<<He>> covers the worst split with tape, then reaches for your record. "I'm writing down what I found. These aren't little scratches."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<He>> picks up a pen but waits before writing. "How did you get these injuries?"
<br><br>
<<link [[Tell <<him>> the truth|Colosseum Nurse Truth]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Say you fell|Colosseum Nurse Lie]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Colosseum Nurse Truth
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "school">><<schooleffects>><<effects>><<person1>><<speechresolve>>
<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
	<<case "meek">>"I've been fighting for money," you say. "I keep going back."
	<<case "shy">>"I... fight at an underground arena," you say. "They pay me for it."
	<<case "polite">>"I'll tell you the truth. I've been fighting for money, and I've gone back more than once," you say.
	<<case "confident">>"I fight for money," you say. "It pays better than the other work I can get."
	<<case "bratty">>"I fight for money," you say. "Rent doesn't pay itself."
	<<case "docile">>"I'm sorry. I've been fighting for money, and I keep going back," you say.
	<<case "cruel">>"I hit people. They pay me. This time I took a few back," you say.
	<<default>>"I've been fighting for money," you say. "I need what they pay me."
<</switch>>
<br><br>
<<He>> writes down what you say without interrupting.
"And how much of that money do you get to keep?" <<He>> waits, then puts the record aside when you do not answer. "You can come here. You don't have to wait until you can barely walk."
<<set $xchange.colosseum.nurseKnows to 1>>
<br><br>
Once the note is finished, <<he>> cleans and treats the injuries properly. <<He>> keeps working even after the bell rings.<<pain -25>><<llpain>><<stress -8>><<llstress>><<trauma -3>><<ltrauma>>
<<set $xchange.colosseum.injuryDays to Math.max(0, $xchange.colosseum.injuryDays - 1)>>
<<if $xchange.colosseum.injuryDays is 0>><<set $xchange.colosseum.injury to 0>><</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Leave|Hallways]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Colosseum Nurse Lie
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "school">><<schooleffects>><<effects>><<person1>><<speechresolve>>
<<pass 10>>
<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
	<<case "meek">>"I fell down the steps outside," you say.
	<<case "shy">>"I... fell down the steps," you say.
	<<case "confident">>"I fell down the steps. That's what happened," you say.
	<<case "bratty">>"I fell down the steps," you say. "Can you just treat it?"
	<<case "docile">>"I fell down the steps," you say. "I'm fine."
	<<case "cruel">>"I fell. That's all you need to know," you say.
	<<default>>"I fell down the steps outside," you say.
<</switch>>
<br><br>
The nurse writes a short note, then turns the sheet away from you.
"Down the steps," <<he>> repeats. <<He>> points to the split skin across your right knuckles. "How did falling do this?"
<br><br>
You do not answer. <<He>> gives you ice, tapes the injury, and stops asking questions.<<pain -12>><<llpain>><<stress 4>><<gstress>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Leave|Hallways]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Colosseum Doren Lunch
<<endevent>><<set $daily.colosseumDorenLunch to 1>>
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "school">><<schooleffects>><<effects>>
<<npc Doren>><<person1>>
Doren is eating lunch at the end of the staff table. When <<he>> sees you approach, <<he>> moves <<his>> bag off the empty chair beside <<him>>, making room for you to sit.
<br><br>
<<if $xchange.colosseum.nurseKnows>>
	"Your name was in a report from the infirmary this morning," <<he>> says while continuing to eat. "I'm not going to question you about it in a room full of other students."
<<else>>
	<<He>> spends the first part of lunch explaining what you missed in the last lesson and does not ask about your bruises.
<</if>>
<br><br>
After you have been sitting together for a while, Doren puts part of <<his>> lunch nearer to you.
"You don't have to tell me what happened... I would rather make sure you eat something."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Colosseum Doren Lunch 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Colosseum Doren Lunch 2
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "school">><<schooleffects>><<effects>><<pass 5>>
You eat while Doren talks about a book <<he>> is halfway through. <<He>> does not return to the subject of your injuries.
<<set $daily.school.lunchEaten to 1>><<stress -10>><<lllstress>><<trauma -5>><<lltrauma>><<npcincr Doren love 1>><<glove>>
<br><br>
When <<he>> is done, <<he>> takes a sheet from <<his>> folder, writes a short note, folds it once, and gives it to you.
"You have an open cut on your hand, so you're not swimming today. Give this to whoever takes the register."
<<set $daily.school.swimmingExcused to true>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Leave|Canteen]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Colosseum Street Hunt
<<set $daily.colosseumHunt to 1>>
<<colosseumHuntNpc>>
<<set $xchange.colosseum.huntReturn to $passage>>
You notice the same footsteps behind you after two turns. Whoever is following you keeps the same distance instead of trying to pass.
<br><br>
You walk faster. The footsteps speed up as well. When you cross the road, the <<person>> crosses after you. On the next turn, <<he>> follows immediately.
<br><br>
<<if _colosseumHunt gte 3>>
	"You let four fighters out through the delivery door," <<he>> calls after you. "The house sent me because it cannot let people think there are no consequences."
<<elseif _colosseumHunt is 2>>
	"You left the Colosseum owing money," the <<person>> says. "They want it dealt with."
<<else>>
	"You kept money you were supposed to return," the <<person>> says. "I was sent to remind you."
<</if>>
<<stress 8>><<ggstress>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Turn around|Colosseum Hunt Start]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Run for it|Colosseum Hunt Run]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Colosseum Hunt Run
<<set $outside to 1>><<effects>><<pass 2>>
You run to the end of the street and turn into the next one. Before you can reach the next corner, a hand grabs the back of your collar and jerks you to a stop.
<br><br>
The <<person>> pulls you around to face <<him>>. <<He>> is breathing steadily despite the chase.
"You were warned."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Colosseum Hunt Start]]>><<set $phase to "ran">><</link>>
<br>

:: Colosseum Hunt Start
<<set $outside to 1>><<effects>>
<<controlloss>><<violence 1>><<neutral 1>><<maninit>>
<<set $enemyanger += 150>><<pass 1>>
<<if $phase is "ran">>
	<<unset $phase>>
	You steady yourself while <<he>> grips your collar. You raise your hands, ready to fight. <<He>> lets go and steps back, raising <<his>> hands as well.
<<else>>
	You stop and turn before <<he>> reaches you. <<He>> stops a short distance away and raises <<his>> hands, ready to fight.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<He>> attacks without another word.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Colosseum Hunt Fight]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Colosseum Hunt Fight
<<effects>><<effectsman>><<man>><<stateman>>
<br><br>
<<actionsman>>
<<if _combatend>>
	<span id="next"><<link [[Next|Colosseum Hunt Result]]>><</link>></span><<nexttext>>
<<else>>
	<span id="next"><<link [[Next|Colosseum Hunt Fight]]>><</link>></span><<nexttext>>
<</if>>

:: Colosseum Hunt Result
<<effects>><<pass 5>>
<<set _victory to $enemyhealth lte 0 or $enemypleasure gte $enemypleasuremax>>
<<set _return to $xchange.colosseum.huntReturn or "Industrial Alleyways">>
<<if _victory>>
	<<colosseumHuntEase>>
	The person sent after you falls against a parked car and slides to the ground. Your attacker tries to stand, but cannot stay upright.
	<br><br>
	You leave without searching their pockets.<<famescrap `6 + $xchange.colosseum.rank * 2` "none" true>><<stress -4>><<lstress>>
<<else>>
	You end up on the ground with your arms covering your head. The attacker keeps kicking until the beating stops, then searches your pockets.
	<<colosseumInjure 2 3>><<trauma 4>><<gtrauma>>
	<br><br>
	<<set _lifted to Math.min($money, 40000)>>
	<<if _lifted gt 0>>
		<<money `-_lifted` "colosseumDebt">>
		The attacker takes <span class="gold"><<printmoney _lifted>></span>, counts it where you can see, then leaves.
	<<else>>
		The attacker finds no money and leaves you on the ground.
	<</if>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<clotheson>><<endcombat>>
<<unset $xchange.colosseum.huntReturn>>
<<link "Next" _return>><<set $eventskip to 1>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Colosseum Outside Challenge
<<effects>><<effectsman>><<man>><<stateman>>
<br><br>
<<actionsman>>
<<if _combatend>>
	<span id="next"><<link [[Next|Colosseum Outside Challenge Result]]>><</link>></span><<nexttext>>
<<else>>
	<span id="next"><<link [[Next|Colosseum Outside Challenge]]>><</link>></span><<nexttext>>
<</if>>

:: Colosseum Outside Challenge Result
<<effects>><<pass 5>>
<<set _victory to $enemyhealth lte 0 or $enemypleasure gte $enemypleasuremax>>
<<if _victory>>
	The person who challenged you falls against the wall. The others who were watching step back instead of joining the fight.
	<br><br>
	<<if $fame.scrap gte 400>>As they leave the alley, one of them tells the others that you are <span class="pink"><<colosseumName>></span>. Nobody questions it.<</if>>
	<<famescrap `4 + $xchange.colosseum.rank` "none" true>><<colosseumHeat 2>>
<<else>>
	You end up on the wet ground with your arms covering your head. The attackers kick you several more times before leaving.
	<br><br>
	<<set _lifted to Math.min($money, 12000)>>
	<<if _lifted gt 0>>
		One of them searches your pockets and takes <span class="gold"><<printmoney _lifted>></span>.<<money `-_lifted` "colosseumDebt">>
	<<else>>
		One of them searches your pockets, finds no money, and shoves your empty wallet back at you.
	<</if>>
	<<colosseumInjure 2 3>><<trauma 3>><<gtrauma>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<clotheson>><<endcombat>>
<<link [[Leave|Industrial Alleyways]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Pub Colosseum Recognition
<<generate1>><<person1>>
<<set $daily.colosseumPubRecognition to 1>>
A <<person>> at the bar notices you and stops before taking a drink.
<<if $xchange.colosseum.quits gte 1>>
	"You're the fighter who surrendered! I had four grand riding on you, then you stopped the fight."
	<br><br>
	The two people beside <<him>> hear the complaint. One of them laughs. Landry glances over from further down the bar, then goes back to serving another customer.
	<<stress 8>><<ggstress>><<trauma 3>><<gtrauma>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Leave|Pub]]>><<endevent>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<if $xchange.colosseum.injuryDays gt 0>>
		<<He>> looks over your injuries.
		<br><br>
		"I saw that fight," <<he>> says. "I had money on it, but I'm not telling you which side I picked."
	<<elseif $fame.scrap gte 400>>
		<br><br>
		"That's <span class="pink"><<colosseumName>></span>," <<he>> says to the person beside <<him>>. "I saw one of your fights.
		The crowd was shouting so loudly the bookmaker could barely hear the bets."
	<<else>>
		<br><br>
		"You fight at the Colosseum under the old factory," <<he>> says. "Don't worry. A lot of people here already know about it."
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<He>> offers to buy you a drink. Landry notices, but leaves the conversation to you.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Accept|Pub Colosseum Drink]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Decline|Pub]]>><<endevent>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>
<</if>>
<br>

:: Pub Colosseum Drink
<<effects>><<pass 10>>
You accept the drink. While you drink, <<he>> talks about one of your recent fights. <<He>> remembers most of it correctly, but exaggerates two parts to make you sound better than you were.
You let <<him>> keep the better version.
<br><br>
After a while, <<he>> leans closer. "Who should I bet on next week?"
<br><br>
<<link [[Tell <<him>> the truth|Pub Colosseum Drink End]]>><<set $xchange.colosseum.tipGiven to "honest">><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Send <<him>> the wrong way|Pub Colosseum Drink End]]>><<set $xchange.colosseum.tipGiven to "lie">><</link>>

:: Pub Colosseum Drink End
<<effects>><<person1>><<pass 5>><<speechresolve>>
<<if $xchange.colosseum.tipGiven is "lie">>
	You name a fighter you expect to lose.
	<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
		<<case "meek">>"I think they're worth betting on," you say, without adding anything else.
		<<case "shy">>"Maybe try them," you say.
		<<case "polite">>"If you want my suggestion, I'd bet on them," you say.
		<<case "confident">>"That's where I'd put the money," you say.
		<<case "bratty">>"You asked for a tip. That's the one you're getting," you say.
		<<case "docile">>"I think they're your best choice," you say.
		<<case "cruel">>"Bet on them. If you lose, that's your problem," you say.
		<<default>>"Bet on them," you say.
	<</switch>>
	<br><br>
	<<He>> writes the name on a receipt and thanks you.
	<<set $xchange.colosseum.dirtyFights += 1>><<colosseumHeat 2>>
<<else>>
	You name the fighter you honestly think is more likely to win.
	<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
		<<case "meek">>"I think they have the better chance," you say. "But I could be wrong."
		<<case "shy">>"Maybe them," you say. "I'm not completely sure."
		<<case "confident">>"They're the better bet," you say. "Nothing is guaranteed."
		<<case "bratty">>"Them," you say. "Don't blame me if they lose."
		<<case "docile">>"I think they have the better chance," you say. "Please don't bet more than you can afford."
		<<case "flamboyant">>"I'd choose them, but don't treat that as a guarantee," you say.
		<<case "cruel">>"Bet on them if you want. I don't care what you lose," you say.
		<<default>>"I'd bet on them," you say. "I could still be wrong."
	<</switch>>
	<br><br>
	<<He>> writes the name down.
	<<colosseumHeat 1>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<unset $xchange.colosseum.tipGiven>>
While <<he>> looks over the name, you finish your drink.<<drunk 40>><<gdrunk>><<stress -3>><<lstress>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Leave|Pub]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Brothel Colosseum Recognition
<<generate1>><<person1>>
<<set $daily.colosseumBrothelRecognition to 1>>
A <<person>> carrying a tray stops in front of you and waits until you look at <<him>>.
<br><br>
"You're the fighter from the Colosseum," <<he>> says. <<He>> shifts the tray to one side. "A lot of the customers downstairs have been betting on you.
One of them says they helped arrange your next match, so they already know who you're fighting."
<br><br>
<<link [[Ask what they've heard|Brothel Colosseum Tip]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Say nothing|Brothel]]>><<endevent>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>
<br>

:: Brothel Colosseum Tip
<<effects>><<person1>><<pass 5>>
<<He>> gives you the patron's name and tells you where that person usually drinks. Then <<he>> adds that your next opponent has visited the Colosseum medical room twice this month.
<br><br>
<<if $xchange.colosseum.briarWatch and !$xchange.colosseum.briarReported>>
	Before continuing, <<he>> checks the stairs to make sure nobody from the office is coming down.
	<br><br>
	"I fight there too, when they book me." <<He>> grips the tray with both hands. "Briar doesn't know. I'm trying to earn enough money to stop before <<he>> finds out."
	<<colosseumHeat 3 "You now know one of Briar's staff is secretly fighting at the Colosseum.">>
<<else>>
	<<He>> leaves to continue serving customers once <<he>> has given you the information.
<</if>>
<<set $xchange.colosseum.insideTip to 1>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Leave|Brothel]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Wren Colosseum Tip
<<set $outside to 0>><<effects>><<speechresolve>>
<<pass 5>>
<<set $daily.colosseumWrenTip to 1>>
<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
	<<case "meek">>"Do you know anything about the Colosseum under the factory?" you ask Wren.
	<<case "shy">>"Um... do you know anything about the Colosseum under the factory?" you ask Wren.
	<<case "confident">>"You know things about the Colosseum. What can you tell me?" you ask Wren.
	<<case "bratty">>"You know more about the Colosseum than you're saying. What is it?" you ask Wren.
	<<case "docile">>"If you can tell me anything about the Colosseum, I'd like to know," you say.
	<<case "flamboyant">>"Can I ask what you know about the Colosseum under the factory?" you ask Wren.
	<<case "cruel">>"What do you know about the Colosseum?" you ask Wren.
	<<default>>"What do you know about the Colosseum under the factory?" you ask Wren.
<</switch>>
<br><br>
"More than you," <<he>> says.
<br><br>
<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
	<<case "meek">>"Do you know anything that could help with my next fight?" you ask.
	<<case "shy">>"Anything about my next opponent?" you ask.
	<<case "confident">>"Give me something useful about my next opponent," you say.
	<<case "bratty">>"Then prove it. Tell me something useful about my next opponent," you say.
	<<case "docile">>"If you can help, I'd like to know about my next opponent," you say.
	<<case "flamboyant">>"Could you tell me anything useful about my next opponent?" you ask.
	<<case "cruel">>"Then tell me what you know about my next opponent," you say.
	<<default>>"What do you know about my next opponent?" you ask.
<</switch>>
<br><br>
"A bad knee," Wren says. "Still fights on it, and puts the weight on the other leg from the first minute. Make them move around for four or five minutes and the bad knee starts giving way."
<<He>> pauses.
"Almost nobody at the Colosseum knows about it. Someone pays to keep it quiet."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Wren Colosseum Tip 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Wren Colosseum Tip 2
<<set $outside to 0>><<effects>><<speechresolve>>
<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
	<<case "meek">>"W-Who told you?" you ask.
	<<case "shy">>"Can I ask who told you?" you ask.
	<<case "confident">>"Who is paying to keep it quiet?" you ask.
	<<case "bratty">>"And who told you all that?" you ask.
	<<case "docile">>"If you can tell me, who did you hear it from?" you ask.
	<<case "flamboyant">>"Who gave you that information?" you ask.
	<<default>>"Who told you?" you ask.
<</switch>>
<br><br>
"The people who pay me." Wren looks at you. "The injury is the tip. Who told me is not.
Use it if you want. Start asking where I got it, and I stop being useful to you."
<<set $xchange.colosseum.insideTip to 1>><<colosseumHeat 3>>
<br><br>
<<if $wrenTalkLocation is "estate">>
	<<link [[Back to the table|Estate Cards Intro]]>><<unset $wrenTalkLocation>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<elseif $wrenTalkLocation is "gambling">>
	<<link [[Back to the ring|Pub Gambling Wren]]>><<unset $wrenTalkLocation>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<link [[Back|Smuggler Pub Wren]]>><<unset $wrenTalkLocation>><</link>>
<</if>>
<br>

:: Shopping Centre Colosseum Patron
<<effects>><<generate1>><<person1>>
<<set $daily.colosseumShoppingRecognition to 1>>
A well-dressed <<person>> notices you while passing through the shopping centre. <<He>> stops and approaches you with an excited smile.
"You're the fighter from the Colosseum, aren't you? My partner won four grand betting on you."
<br><br>
<<He>> speaks loud that a few nearby shoppers hear. They glance over, curious about what <<he>> means.<<stress 6>><<ggstress>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Shopping Centre Colosseum Patron Talk]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Shopping Centre Colosseum Patron Talk
<<effects>>
You let <<him>> continue. <<He>> talks excitedly about your recent fights, using your arena name often for nearby shoppers to notice.
<br><br>
A few people stop to listen. One of them recognises you and raises a phone to record.
<br><br>
Before leaving, the <<person>> presses <span class="gold"><<printmoney 20000>></span> into your hand.
<<money 20000 "colosseum">><<fameexhibitionism 8 "none" true>><<famescrap 6 "none" true>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Leave|Shopping Centre]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Smuggler Pub Colosseum Recognition
<<generate1>><<person1>>
<<set $daily.colosseumSmugglerRecognition to 1>>
<<if $xchange.colosseum.story is 2 and $xchange.colosseum.rank gte 3>><<colosseumHeat 2>><</if>>
<<if $xchange.colosseum.dirtyFights gte 2>>
	A card player covers the coins on the table as you pass. "Don't trust that one with a fixed fight," <<he>> tells the others.
<<elseif $xchange.colosseum.fixes gte 2>>
	A bookmaker raises two fingers in greeting. "That one's reliable. Pay them to lose, and they'll lose." Someone at the table immediately asks when your next fight is.
<<elseif $xchange.colosseum.protects gte 2>>
	A fighter with a split eyebrow pushes an empty chair towards you. "Sit down. You helped me when two people tried to gang up on me last week." The person beside <<him>> stops complaining and makes room.
<<elseif $xchange.colosseum.losses gte 3 and $xchange.colosseum.losses gte $xchange.colosseum.wins>>
	Someone raises a glass towards you. "That's the fighter who keeps coming back even after losing." A few others tap their glasses against the table until you acknowledge them.
<<elseif $xchange.colosseum.wins gte $xchange.colosseum.losses + 5>>
	One smuggler looks ready to bother you as you pass, but the person beside <<him>> stops <<him>>. "Leave <<pher stranger>> alone. <<pShe stranger>> win most of their fights."
<<elseif $xchange.colosseum.rank gte 5>>
	A stranger recognises you and quickly moves <<his>> chair out of your way. "Sorry. Didn't realise it was you."
<<else>>
	Two smugglers stop talking when you pass. Once you are a few steps away, one says your arena name to the other. They have started to recognise you.
<</if>>
<<endevent>>
<br><br>

:: Bailey Colosseum Cut
<<set $weekly.colosseumBaileyCut to true>>
Bailey already has the ledger open when you reach the desk.
"How many fights did you have this week?"
<br><br>
You tell <<him>>. Bailey writes the number beside your name, calculates what you owe <<him>>, then shows you the total.
<<if $xchange.colosseum.injuryDays gt 0>>
	"You're injured, so I know you can't earn as much right now."
<<elseif $xchange.colosseum.debt gt 0>>
	"One of the Colosseum's collectors came looking for you. They said you owe them money." Bailey taps the ledger with <<his>> pen. "Pay that debt before they come back here."
<<else>>
	"I don't care how you make the money. Just make sure I get my share."
<</if>>
<br><br>

:: Industrial Colosseum Rumour
<<generate1>><<generate2>><<person1>><<person2>>
Two people are smoking beside a loading bay. As you pass, you hear one of them mention a £2,000 payment for a fight.
You slow down and move behind a stack of pallets to listen.
<br><br>
"Even F-rank fighters get paid when they lose," the <<person1>><<person>> says. "That's why so many new people sign up."
<br><br>
The <<person2>><<person>> takes the cigarette. "Yeah, if they come back out. Danny went in for another fight and hasn't been seen since. The landlord's been round asking about the rent."
<br><br>
The first person glances towards the old factory. "Maybe Danny finally went too far."
<br><br>
<<set $skulduggerydifficulty to 300>>
<<link [[Keep listening|Industrial Colosseum Rumour Listen]]>><</link>><<skulduggerydifficulty>>
<br>
<<link [[Move on|Industrial Alleyways]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Industrial Colosseum Rumour Listen
<<effects>><<pass 5>>
<<set $skulduggerydifficulty to 300>>
<<skulduggerycheck "silent">>
<<if $skulduggerysuccess isnot 1>>
	You lower yourself behind the pallets, but one of them shifts against the wall.<<stress 6>><<ggstress>>
	<br><br>
	Their conversation stops. One of them walks towards the noise and checks behind the crates near the end of the loading bay. You keep your head down until their footsteps move away again.
	<br><br>
	"See anything?" the other asks.
	<br><br>
	"Nah. Probably just this place falling apart." They both glance back towards the pallets. "Come on. Finish your smoke. I don't want to hang around here all night."
	<br><br>
	The other person takes one last drag before dropping the cigarette and crushing it under the shoe. They leave through the yard gate together, taking the rest of their conversation with them.
	<<set $daily.colosseumRumourFail to 1>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Leave|Industrial Alleyways]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<<set $xchange.colosseum.heard to 1>>
	You stay crouched behind the pallets and listen.
	<br><br>
	"They still running those fights at the old factory?" one of them asks.
	<br><br>
	"Yeah. Place hasn't changed much."<br>
	"Oh? Fighters in the pit, else throwing money from the seats."<br>
	"Pretty much. Only front door's shut now."<br>
	"What about the passphrase?"<br>
	<br>
	The other shrugs. "Don't know it. Ask Landry. <<nnpc_He "Landry">> can probably get it for you."
	<br><br>
	The taller one snorts. "Huh, sounds like <<nnpc_him "Landry">>. <<nnpc_He "Landry">> knows shit about me I don't remember telling anyone."
	<br><br>
	They continue talking as they walk towards the main road, but you cannot hear them clearly from behind the pallets. You stay where you are until their voices are gone, then leave your hiding place.
	<<skulduggeryskilluse>><br><br>
	<<link [[Leave|Industrial Alleyways]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><<endevent>><</link>>
<</if>>
<br>

:: Pub Landry Colosseum
<<endevent>><<pass 5>>
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "pub">><<effects>><<npc Landry>><<person1>><<speechresolve>>
<<set $xchange.colosseum.route to "landry">>
You wait until Landry is free, then ask <<him>> about the underground fights beneath the old factory.
"Who told you about that?"
<br><br>
<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
	<<case "meek">>"I overheard some people talking about it in the industrial district," you say. "They mentioned your name."
	<<case "shy">>"I... overheard people talking about it," you say. "They said you knew how to get in."
	<<case "confident">>"Nobody told me directly. I overheard them, and they said you knew how to get in," you say.
	<<case "bratty">>"Nobody," you say. "I overheard people talking. They said you knew how to get in."
	<<case "docile">>"I wasn't trying to cause trouble," you say. "I overheard people talking, and they mentioned you."
	<<case "flamboyant">>"I overheard a conversation in the industrial district," you say. "They said you might know how to get inside."
	<<case "cruel">>"Nobody. I overheard them. They said you knew the entrance," you say.
	<<default>>"I overheard people talking in the industrial district. They said you knew the way inside," you say.
<</switch>>
<br><br>
Landry looks around before leaning closer. "Behind the old factory, there's a steel door hidden behind a skip. Knock twice.
When someone opens the panel, say <span class="gold">'The strongest of the studs breeds even the weakest.'</span>"
<br><br>
<<He>> points at you. "Say it exactly like that. If you get it wrong, they won't let you in."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Pub Landry Colosseum Warning]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Pub Landry Colosseum Warning
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "pub">><<effects>>
<<if $fame.scrap lt 1200>>
	"You're not known enough yet," Landry says. "The guard won't let you in unless they've already heard you can fight. Build your reputation first."
	<br><br>
<</if>>
<<if playerAwareTheyArePregnant()>>
	<<if playerBellyVisible(true)>>Landry looks at your belly.<<else>>You tell Landry that you are pregnant.<</if>> "They won't let you fight while you're pregnant. You'll have to wait."
	<br><br>
<</if>>
You turn to leave, but Landry grabs your sleeve before you can step away. "One more thing. If you lose, take your pay and leave. Don't argue with the staff or cause trouble with the bettors.
They'll protect the Colosseum before they protect you."
<br><br>
Landry still has hold of your sleeve. "And think about what losing means there. The winner doesn't just beat you. Somebody ends up carrying what comes after, and then somebody has to raise it. You can't undo that, and it's yours to look after."
<br><br>
Landry lets go. "Danny caused trouble after a fight. Nobody around here has seen Danny since."
<<set $xchange.colosseum.keyKnown to 1>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Back|Pub]]>><<set $phase to 1>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Briar Underground Colosseum
<<endevent>><<pass 5>>
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "brothel">><<effects>><<npc Briar>><<person1>><<speechresolve>>
<<set $xchange.colosseum.route to "briar">>
You ask Briar if the rumours about an underground fighting arena in the industrial district are true.
<br><br>
"They're true," Briar says. "One of my regulars dropped twenty grand betting there, then came here and spent the rest of the night talking about it."
<br><br>
<<He>> puts <<his>> drink down. "I'd rather that money was being spent here."
<br><br>
You ask how to get inside.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Briar Underground Colosseum 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Briar Underground Colosseum 2
<<effects>><<npc Briar>><<person1>><<speechresolve>>
<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
	<<case "meek">>"If you don't want to tell me, that's fine," you say. "I just wanted to know."
	<<case "shy">>"Could you tell me how to get in?" you ask.
	<<case "confident">>"You know the entrance. Tell me where it is," you say.
	<<case "bratty">>"You know how to get in," you say. "Just tell me."
	<<case "docile">>"If you're willing to tell me, I'd like to know how to get in," you say.
	<<case "flamboyant">>"Would you tell me how to get inside?" you ask.
	<<case "cruel">>"Tell me how to get in," you say.
	<<default>>"So how do I get in?" you ask.
<</switch>>
<br><br>
"Go behind the old factory. There's a steel door beside a large rubbish container. Give them this passphrase."
<br><br>
"It's a joint project between a few businesses round here," Briar adds. "The rich come to watch people fight and breed, and they keep coming back. I'm not the only one who gets a cut." <<He>> looks at your stomach and then away. "If you come out of it with a bump, working for me gets harder. Think about that before you go."
<br><br>
Briar tells you the phrase, then makes you repeat it. You get one word wrong, so <<he>> corrects you and has you try again.
<br><br>
Before you leave, Briar stops you. "Last one. If you see any of my workers fighting or working there, get their names for me.
I want to know if they're taking Colosseum jobs without telling me."
<<set $xchange.colosseum.keyKnown to 1>><<set $xchange.colosseum.briarWatch to 1>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Back|Briar's Office]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Bailey Underground Colosseum
<<endevent>><<pass 5>>
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "home">><<effects>><<npc Bailey>><<person1>><<speechresolve>>
<<set $xchange.colosseum.route to "bailey">>
You ask Bailey about the underground arena in the industrial district.
<br><br>
Bailey does not look up from the paperwork. "No."
<br><br>
You remain by the desk.
<br><br>
<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
	<<case "meek">>"I just want to know if it's real," you say. "Please?"
	<<case "shy">>You hesitate before speaking again. "Could you at least tell me if it's real?"
	<<case "confident">>"You know where it is," you say. "Just tell me."
	<<case "bratty">>"You already know what I'm asking," you say. "So answer me."
	<<case "docile">>"I won't cause trouble," you say. "I just want to know where it is."
	<<case "flamboyant">>"I understand the dramatic refusal," you say. "Now could you tell me where it is?"
	<<case "cruel">>"Stop wasting my time and tell me," you say.
	<<default>>"I'm asking anyway," you say.
<</switch>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Bailey Underground Colosseum 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Bailey Underground Colosseum 2
<<effects>>
Bailey finally puts the pen down. "Go behind the old factory. There's an unmarked steel door. Knock twice."
<br><br>
<<He>> tells you the passphrase, then makes you repeat it. You get one word wrong, so <<he>> corrects you.
"Learn it properly. If you say the wrong thing at the door, they'll think you're police, and I'm not coming to get you."
<br><br>
As you turn to leave, Bailey adds, "And if you make money fighting there, I get my share first. The last two who went in for the money came out owing me extra rent, because somebody had put a child in them that I hadn't agreed to house."
<<set $xchange.colosseum.keyKnown to 1>><<set $xchange.colosseum.baileyKnows to 1>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Back|Bailey's Office]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Brothel Colosseum Receptionist
<<colosseumHost>>
<<set $daily.colosseumBrothelHost to 1>>
The Colosseum's receptionist is at a table near the stage, off duty and without the book. Two of Briar's workers are on the stage, and the receptionist is watching them with both hands flat on the table and both knees pressed together. Every few seconds the knees shift.
<br><br>
When <<he>> notices you, <<he>> does not look away from the stage for a full second. Then <<he>> lifts a glass. "I can't help it. Give me two people who mean it and I'm useless for an hour."
<br><br>
<<link [[Sit with <<him>>|Brothel Colosseum Receptionist Talk]]>><</link>>
